{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run inventory-api on node1 as a managed service listening on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A boot-enabled SysV service was installed and started under the dedicated inventory-api account. Direct checks show its Python process listening on TCP 8080 and returning HTTP 200 for health and inventory requests. After a bounded reboot, it returned automatically with a new PID, listener, health response, and inventory response.","evidence_ids":["cmd-18465fd998a24599","cmd-694ddb34610f483f","cmd-ebf9fffc18d64c45","cmd-a75fd96c84a5439e","cmd-351241b458ab4b84","cmd-983c993bb48b4440"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Limit the separate batchworker account to 128 MB of virtual memory per process, and ensure a failed batch allocation does not interrupt the API.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The distinct batchworker account was created and configured with matching 131072 KiB soft and hard address-space limits. Sessions directly reported that limit; a 192 MB Python allocation failed with MemoryError while the API retained the same PID and remained healthy. The limit and isolation behavior were demonstrated again after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f409b724c314ca1","cmd-126ea257e9da4dc0","cmd-304c3c5e5b4c48e3","cmd-983c993bb48b4440","cmd-99bcca7c3a7340c5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were observed before the changes and remained present after implementation and reboot. The service uses the installed Python 2.5.1, passed bytecode compilation, and operated successfully before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a43cf15c6aa744b0","cmd-1e2b7ba9adc94b5f","cmd-5d699867719c4e84","cmd-983c993bb48b4440","cmd-99bcca7c3a7340c5","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account creation, application and init-script installation, startup links, PAM/limits configuration, service start, compatibility compilation, and reboot all have clear roles in the requested outcomes or mandatory restart verification. Temporary HTTP response and reboot-log files were bounded evidence artifacts, and the final temporary-files snapshot was empty. Package-manager consistency remained healthy. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart service/data/limit state, acknowledgement, observed SSH disruption, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data/limit state; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f409b724c314ca1","cmd-5d699867719c4e84","cmd-18465fd998a24599","cmd-126ea257e9da4dc0","cmd-36a5164d3b764d34","cmd-694ddb34610f483f","cmd-ebf9fffc18d64c45","cmd-6d7ddd6b359c4446","cmd-a75fd96c84a5439e","cmd-351241b458ab4b84","cmd-983c993bb48b4440","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct runtime and post-reboot evidence. The API is managed and healthy on TCP 8080, the batchworker limit is enforced without affecting the API, the legacy OS/kernel were retained, and the mandatory node-restart protocol was completed coherently.","limitations":["The generic after-executor listening-sockets lifecycle observation was empty despite direct contemporaneous commands showing the TCP 8080 listener; the direct service, socket, and HTTP probes provide the stronger task-specific evidence.","Systemd failed-unit inspection was unsupported on this SysV-based legacy platform, so hygiene relies on direct service checks and package-health observations."]}
